-- Sale of Goods Act 1979 (Singapore), 2020 RE, informal consolidation in force from 1/4/2022.
-- LAYER 1, PART 6: ACTIONS FOR BREACH OF THE CONTRACT (ss 49 to 54).
-- JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE are answers the text gives in its own words; NOTHING is "the Act does not answer on
-- these facts".  A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Money amounts are plain NUMBERs.  "Estimated loss", "available market" and "market or current price" are
-- findings of fact supplied by the caller, not computed by the Act.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `soga-nouns`

DECLARE `Form of a judgment or decree for specific performance` IS ONE OF
    `unconditional`
    `on such terms and conditions as to damages, payment of the price and otherwise as seem just to the court`
    `some other form`

DECLARE `Matter that section 54 leaves untouched` IS ONE OF
    `the right of the buyer or the seller to recover interest in a case where by law interest may be recoverable`
    `the right of the buyer or the seller to recover special damages in a case where by law special damages may be recoverable`
    `the right of the buyer or the seller to recover money paid where the consideration for the payment of it has failed`
    `some other matter under section 54`

§ `Part 6 -- Actions for breach of the contract`

§§ `Seller's remedies (ss 49 and 50)`

-- s 49(1).
-- src:1340 | 49.—(1) Where, under a contract of sale, the property in the goods
-- src:1341 | has passed to the buyer and he wrongfully neglects or refuses to pay
-- src:1342 | for the goods according to the terms of the contract, the seller may
-- src:1343 | maintain an action against him for the price of the goods.
@ref s 49(1) (src:1340-1343)
GIVEN `under the contract of sale the property in the goods has passed to the buyer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the buyer wrongfully neglects or refuses to pay for the goods according to the terms of the contract` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 49(1) the seller may maintain an action against the buyer for the price of the goods` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `under the contract of sale the property in the goods has passed to the buyer` AND `the buyer wrongfully neglects or refuses to pay for the goods according to the terms of the contract`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the subsection applies "Where, under a contract of sale, the property in the goods has passed to the buyer and he wrongfully neglects or refuses to pay"; s 49(2) is a second route. -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
            JUST FALSE

-- s 49(2).
-- src:1345 | (2) Where, under a contract of sale, the price is payable on a day
-- src:1346 | certain irrespective of delivery and the buyer wrongfully neglects or
-- src:1347 | refuses to pay such price, the seller may maintain an action for the
-- src:1348 | price, although the property in the goods has not passed and the goods
-- src:1349 | have not been appropriated to the contract.
@ref s 49(2) (src:1345-1349)
GIVEN `under the contract of sale the price is payable on a day certain irrespective of delivery` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the buyer wrongfully neglects or refuses to pay such price` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 49(2) the seller may maintain an action for the price although the property in the goods has not passed and the goods have not been appropriated to the contract` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `under the contract of sale the price is payable on a day certain irrespective of delivery` AND `the buyer wrongfully neglects or refuses to pay such price`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the subsection applies "Where, under a contract of sale, the price is payable on a day certain irrespective of delivery and the buyer wrongfully neglects or refuses to pay such price". -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
            JUST FALSE

-- ss 49(1) and (2) gathered by hand (E1 option B): the seller's action for the price.
-- src:1340 | 49.—(1) Where, under a contract of sale, the property in the goods
-- src:1341 | has passed to the buyer and he wrongfully neglects or refuses to pay
-- src:1342 | for the goods according to the terms of the contract, the seller may
-- src:1343 | maintain an action against him for the price of the goods.
-- src:1345 | (2) Where, under a contract of sale, the price is payable on a day
-- src:1346 | certain irrespective of delivery and the buyer wrongfully neglects or
-- src:1347 | refuses to pay such price, the seller may maintain an action for the
-- src:1348 | price, although the property in the goods has not passed and the goods
-- src:1349 | have not been appropriated to the contract.
@ref ss 49(1) and (2) (src:1340-1349)
GIVEN `s 49(1) answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 49(2) answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `ss 49(1) and (2) the seller may maintain an action against the buyer for the price` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 49(1) answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `s 49(2) answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the two subsections give two routes; they do not say that there is no other.
            NOTHING

-- s 50(1).
-- src:1353 | 50.—(1) Where the buyer wrongfully neglects or refuses to accept
-- src:1354 | and pay for the goods, the seller may maintain an action against him
-- src:1355 | for damages for non-acceptance.
@ref s 50(1) (src:1353-1355)
GIVEN `the buyer wrongfully neglects or refuses to accept and pay for the goods` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 50(1) the seller may maintain an action against the buyer for damages for non-acceptance` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the buyer wrongfully neglects or refuses to accept and pay for the goods`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the subsection applies "Where the buyer wrongfully neglects or refuses to accept and pay for the goods". -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
            JUST FALSE

-- s 50(2).
-- src:1357 | (2) The measure of damages is the estimated loss directly and
-- src:1358 | naturally resulting, in the ordinary course of events, from the buyer’s
-- src:1359 | breach of contract.
@ref s 50(2) (src:1357-1359)
GIVEN `the buyer wrongfully neglects or refuses to accept and pay for the goods` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the estimated loss directly and naturally resulting, in the ordinary course of events, from the buyer's breach of contract` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 50(2) the measure of damages for non-acceptance` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the buyer wrongfully neglects or refuses to accept and pay for the goods`
        THEN JUST `the estimated loss directly and naturally resulting, in the ordinary course of events, from the buyer's breach of contract`
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the measure is stated for the breach in s 50(1), "the buyer’s breach of contract".
            NOTHING

-- s 50(3).
-- src:1361 | (3) Where there is an available market for the goods in question, the
-- src:1362 | measure of damages is prima facie to be ascertained by the difference
-- src:1363 | between the contract price and the market or current price of the
-- src:1364 | goods at the time or times when they ought to have been accepted or
-- src:1365 | (if no time was fixed for acceptance) at the time of the refusal to
-- src:1366 | accept.
@ref s 50(3) (src:1361-1366)
GIVEN `the buyer wrongfully neglects or refuses to accept and pay for the goods` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is an available market for the goods in question` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is shown` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract price` IS A NUMBER
      `the market or current price of the goods at the time or times when they ought to have been accepted or, if no time was fixed, at the time of the refusal to accept` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 50(3) the measure of damages for non-acceptance where there is an available market` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the buyer wrongfully neglects or refuses to accept and pay for the goods` AND `there is an available market for the goods in question`)
        THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection applies "Where there is an available market for the goods in question". The yes/no twin `s 50(3) the market-price rule for non-acceptance applies` answers JUST FALSE here (ruled 2026-11-05 (b)); a function that returns a value cannot say no.
            NOTHING
        IF `the contrary is shown`
        THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "prima facie" -- the measure yields to proof of the contrary.
            NOTHING
        IF `the contract price` AT LEAST `the market or current price of the goods at the time or times when they ought to have been accepted or, if no time was fixed, at the time of the refusal to accept`
        THEN JUST (`the contract price` MINUS `the market or current price of the goods at the time or times when they ought to have been accepted or, if no time was fixed, at the time of the refusal to accept`)
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "the difference between the contract price and the market or current price" is not signed in the text; where the market price is above the contract price the seller has no shortfall and the subsection does not say whether the measure is nil.
            NOTHING

-- Twin of `s 50(3) the measure of damages for non-acceptance where there is an available market`: yes or no, does the rule apply? (ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if")
-- src:1361 | (3) Where there is an available market for the goods in question, the
-- src:1362 | measure of damages is prima facie to be ascertained by the difference
-- src:1363 | between the contract price and the market or current price of the
-- src:1364 | goods at the time or times when they ought to have been accepted or
-- src:1365 | (if no time was fixed for acceptance) at the time of the refusal to
-- src:1366 | accept.
@ref s 50(3) applies (src:1361-1366)
GIVEN `the buyer wrongfully neglects or refuses to accept and pay for the goods` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is an available market for the goods in question` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 50(3) the market-price rule for non-acceptance applies` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the buyer wrongfully neglects or refuses to accept and pay for the goods` AND `there is an available market for the goods in question`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where there is an available market for the goods in question the measure of damages is prima facie to be ascertained by the difference between the contract price and the market or current price" -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
            JUST FALSE

§§ `Buyer's remedies (ss 51 to 53)`

-- s 51(1).
-- src:1375 | 51.—(1) Where the seller wrongfully neglects or refuses to deliver
-- src:1376 | the goods to the buyer, the buyer may maintain an action against the
-- src:1377 | seller for damages for non-delivery.
@ref s 51(1) (src:1375-1377)
GIVEN `the seller wrongfully neglects or refuses to deliver the goods to the buyer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 51(1) the buyer may maintain an action against the seller for damages for non-delivery` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the seller wrongfully neglects or refuses to deliver the goods to the buyer`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the subsection applies "Where the seller wrongfully neglects or refuses to deliver the goods to the buyer". -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
            JUST FALSE

-- s 51(2).
-- src:1379 | (2) The measure of damages is the estimated loss directly and
-- src:1380 | naturally resulting, in the ordinary course of events, from the seller’s
-- src:1381 | breach of contract.
@ref s 51(2) (src:1379-1381)
GIVEN `the seller wrongfully neglects or refuses to deliver the goods to the buyer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the estimated loss directly and naturally resulting, in the ordinary course of events, from the seller's breach of contract` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 51(2) the measure of damages for non-delivery` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the seller wrongfully neglects or refuses to deliver the goods to the buyer`
        THEN JUST `the estimated loss directly and naturally resulting, in the ordinary course of events, from the seller's breach of contract`
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the measure is stated for the breach in s 51(1), "the seller’s breach of contract".
            NOTHING

-- s 51(3).
-- src:1383 | (3) Where there is an available market for the goods in question, the
-- src:1384 | measure of damages is prima facie to be ascertained by the difference
-- src:1385 | between the contract price and the market or current price of the
-- src:1386 | goods at the time or times when they ought to have been delivered or
-- src:1387 | (if no time was fixed) at the time of the refusal to deliver.
@ref s 51(3) (src:1383-1387)
GIVEN `the seller wrongfully neglects or refuses to deliver the goods to the buyer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is an available market for the goods in question` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is shown` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract price` IS A NUMBER
      `the market or current price of the goods at the time or times when they ought to have been delivered or, if no time was fixed, at the time of the refusal to deliver` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 51(3) the measure of damages for non-delivery where there is an available market` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the seller wrongfully neglects or refuses to deliver the goods to the buyer` AND `there is an available market for the goods in question`)
        THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection applies "Where there is an available market for the goods in question". The yes/no twin `s 51(3) the market-price rule for non-delivery applies` answers JUST FALSE here (ruled 2026-11-05 (b)); a function that returns a value cannot say no.
            NOTHING
        IF `the contrary is shown`
        THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "prima facie" -- the measure yields to proof of the contrary.
            NOTHING
        IF `the market or current price of the goods at the time or times when they ought to have been delivered or, if no time was fixed, at the time of the refusal to deliver` AT LEAST `the contract price`
        THEN JUST (`the market or current price of the goods at the time or times when they ought to have been delivered or, if no time was fixed, at the time of the refusal to deliver` MINUS `the contract price`)
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "the difference between the contract price and the market or current price" is not signed in the text; where the market price is below the contract price the buyer has no shortfall and the subsection does not say whether the measure is nil.
            NOTHING

-- Twin of `s 51(3) the measure of damages for non-delivery where there is an available market`: yes or no, does the rule apply? (ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if")
-- src:1383 | (3) Where there is an available market for the goods in question, the
-- src:1384 | measure of damages is prima facie to be ascertained by the difference
-- src:1385 | between the contract price and the market or current price of the
-- src:1386 | goods at the time or times when they ought to have been delivered or
-- src:1387 | (if no time was fixed) at the time of the refusal to deliver.
@ref s 51(3) applies (src:1383-1387)
GIVEN `the seller wrongfully neglects or refuses to deliver the goods to the buyer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is an available market for the goods in question` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 51(3) the market-price rule for non-delivery applies` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the seller wrongfully neglects or refuses to deliver the goods to the buyer` AND `there is an available market for the goods in question`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where there is an available market for the goods in question the measure of damages is prima facie to be ascertained by the difference between the contract price and the market or current price" -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
            JUST FALSE

-- s 52(1).
-- src:1391 | 52.—(1) In any action for breach of contract to deliver specific or
-- src:1392 | ascertained goods, the court may, if it thinks fit, on the claimant’s
-- src:1393 | application, by its judgment or decree direct that the contract shall be
-- src:1394 | performed specifically, without giving the defendant the option of
-- src:1395 | retaining the goods on payment of damages.
@ref s 52(1) (src:1391-1395)
GIVEN `the action is for breach of contract to deliver specific or ascertained goods` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 52(1) the court has power to direct that the contract shall be performed specifically` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the action is for breach of contract to deliver specific or ascertained goods`
        THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is given "In any action for breach of contract to deliver specific or ascertained goods"; a scope limit with no "only" (ruled 2026-11-05 (c)). Whether the court thinks fit is for the court and is not an input.
            NOTHING
        IF `the claimant applies`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the court may so direct "on the claimant’s application" -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a condition of the grant not met is the text's no, like "if"; the "on the claimant's application" is read as an "if" (assumed, not ruled; fork F10).
            JUST FALSE

-- s 52(2).
-- src:1399 | (2) The claimant’s application may be made at any time before
-- src:1400 | judgment or decree.
@ref s 52(2) (src:1399-1400)
GIVEN `the application is made before judgment or decree` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 52(2) the claimant's application may be made` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the application is made before judgment or decree`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "at any time before judgment or decree" is a stated period; after judgment or decree the application may not be made under this subsection. -- ruled 2026-11-05 (a): a period the text fixes in its own words; outside it the answer is no
            JUST FALSE

-- s 52(3).
-- src:1404 | (3) The judgment or decree may be unconditional, or on such terms
-- src:1405 | and conditions as to damages, payment of the price and otherwise as
-- src:1406 | seem just to the court.
@ref s 52(3) (src:1404-1406)
GIVEN `the form` IS A `Form of a judgment or decree for specific performance`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 52(3) the judgment or decree may take this form` IS
    CONSIDER `the form`
    WHEN `unconditional` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `on such terms and conditions as to damages, payment of the price and otherwise as seem just to the court` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the subsection says the judgment "may be" in two forms and does not say that no other is allowed.
    WHEN `some other form` THEN NOTHING

-- s 53(1), first limb: no right to reject by reason only of the breach of warranty.
-- src:1410 | 53.—(1) Where there is a breach of warranty by the seller, or where
-- src:1411 | the buyer elects (or is compelled) to treat any breach of a condition on
-- src:1412 | the part of the seller as a breach of warranty, the buyer is not by reason
-- src:1413 | only of such breach of warranty entitled to reject the goods; but he
-- src:1414 | may —
@ref s 53(1) reject (src:1410-1414)
GIVEN `there is a breach of warranty by the seller` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the buyer elects or is compelled to treat a breach of a condition on the part of the seller as a breach of warranty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 53(1) the buyer is entitled to reject the goods by reason only of the breach of warranty` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `there is a breach of warranty by the seller` OR `the buyer elects or is compelled to treat a breach of a condition on the part of the seller as a breach of warranty`
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the buyer is not by reason only of such breach of warranty entitled to reject the goods"
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection applies "Where there is a breach of warranty by the seller, or where the buyer elects (or is compelled) to treat any breach of a condition on the part of the seller as a breach of warranty".
            NOTHING

-- s 53(1)(a).
-- src:1410 | 53.—(1) Where there is a breach of warranty by the seller, or where
-- src:1411 | the buyer elects (or is compelled) to treat any breach of a condition on
-- src:1412 | the part of the seller as a breach of warranty, the buyer is not by reason
-- src:1413 | only of such breach of warranty entitled to reject the goods; but he
-- src:1414 | may —
-- src:1419 | (a) set up against the seller the breach of warranty in
-- src:1420 | diminution or extinction of the price; or
@ref s 53(1)(a) (src:1410-1420)
GIVEN `there is a breach of warranty by the seller` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the buyer elects or is compelled to treat a breach of a condition on the part of the seller as a breach of warranty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 53(1)(a) the buyer may set up against the seller the breach of warranty in diminution or extinction of the price` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `there is a breach of warranty by the seller` OR `the buyer elects or is compelled to treat a breach of a condition on the part of the seller as a breach of warranty`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the subsection applies "Where there is a breach of warranty by the seller, or where the buyer elects (or is compelled) to treat any breach of a condition ... as a breach of warranty". -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
            JUST FALSE

-- s 53(1)(b).
-- src:1410 | 53.—(1) Where there is a breach of warranty by the seller, or where
-- src:1411 | the buyer elects (or is compelled) to treat any breach of a condition on
