@ref s 53(1)(b) (src:1410-1414) (src:1422-1423)
GIVEN `there is a breach of warranty by the seller` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the buyer elects or is compelled to treat a breach of a condition on the part of the seller as a breach of warranty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 53(1)(b) the buyer may maintain an action against the seller for damages for the breach of warranty` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `there is a breach of warranty by the seller` OR `the buyer elects or is compelled to treat a breach of a condition on the part of the seller as a breach of warranty`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the subsection applies "Where there is a breach of warranty by the seller, or where the buyer elects (or is compelled) to treat any breach of a condition ... as a breach of warranty". -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
            JUST FALSE

-- s 53(2).
-- src:1425 | (2) The measure of damages for breach of warranty is the estimated
-- src:1426 | loss directly and naturally resulting, in the ordinary course of events,
-- src:1427 | from the breach of warranty.
@ref s 53(2) (src:1425-1427)
GIVEN `there is a breach of warranty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the estimated loss directly and naturally resulting, in the ordinary course of events, from the breach of warranty` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 53(2) the measure of damages for breach of warranty` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `there is a breach of warranty`
        THEN JUST `the estimated loss directly and naturally resulting, in the ordinary course of events, from the breach of warranty`
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the measure is stated "for breach of warranty".
