-- s 53(3).
-- src:1429 | (3) In the case of breach of warranty of quality, such loss is prima
-- src:1430 | facie the difference between the value of the goods at the time of
-- src:1431 | delivery to the buyer and the value they would have had if they had
-- src:1432 | fulfilled the warranty.
@ref s 53(3) (src:1429-1432)
GIVEN `there is a breach of warranty of quality` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is shown` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the value of the goods at the time of delivery to the buyer` IS A NUMBER
      `the value the goods would have had if they had fulfilled the warranty` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 53(3) the loss for breach of warranty of quality` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `there is a breach of warranty of quality`
        THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection applies "In the case of breach of warranty of quality". The yes/no twin `s 53(3) the rule for breach of warranty of quality applies` answers JUST FALSE here (ruled 2026-11-05 (k)); a function that returns a value cannot say no.
            NOTHING
        IF `the contrary is shown`
        THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "prima facie" -- the measure yields to proof of the contrary.
            NOTHING
        IF `the value the goods would have had if they had fulfilled the warranty` AT LEAST `the value of the goods at the time of delivery to the buyer`
        THEN JUST (`the value the goods would have had if they had fulfilled the warranty` MINUS `the value of the goods at the time of delivery to the buyer`)
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the difference is not signed in the text; where the goods were worth more than a conforming set would have been, the subsection does not say whether the loss is nil.
            NOTHING

-- Twin of `s 53(3) the loss for breach of warranty of quality`: yes or no, does the rule apply? (ruled 2026-11-05 (k): "in the case of" read as "where" (assumed, not ruled; fork F10): the condition not met is the text's no)
