        IF `there is a breach of warranty of quality`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In the case of breach of warranty of quality such loss is prima facie the difference between the value of the goods at the time of delivery to the buyer and the value they would have had if they had answered to the warranty" -- ruled 2026-11-05 (k): "in the case of" read as "where" (assumed, not ruled; fork F10): the condition not met is the text's no
            JUST FALSE

-- s 53(4).
-- src:1434 | (4) The fact that the buyer has set up the breach of warranty in
-- src:1435 | diminution or extinction of the price does not prevent him from
-- src:1436 | maintaining an action for the same breach of warranty if he has
-- src:1437 | suffered further damage.
@ref s 53(4) (src:1434-1437)
GIVEN `the buyer has set up the breach of warranty in diminution or extinction of the price` IS A BOOLEAN
      `he has suffered further damage` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 53(4) setting up the breach of warranty in diminution or extinction of the price prevents the buyer from maintaining an action for the same breach` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the buyer has set up the breach of warranty in diminution or extinction of the price` AND `he has suffered further damage`
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not prevent him from maintaining an action for the same breach of warranty if he has suffered further damage"
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection says only that setting up the breach "does not prevent" an action "if he has suffered further damage".
            NOTHING

§§ `Interest, etc. (s 54)`

-- s 54.
-- src:1443 | 54. Nothing in this Act affects the right of the buyer or the seller to
-- src:1444 | recover interest or special damages in any case where by law interest
-- src:1445 | or special damages may be recoverable, or to recover money paid
-- src:1446 | where the consideration for the payment of it has failed.
@ref s 54 (src:1443-1446)
GIVEN `the matter` IS A `Matter that section 54 leaves untouched`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 54 this Act affects the matter` IS
    CONSIDER `the matter`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this Act affects the right of the buyer or the seller to recover interest or special damages in any case where by law interest or special damages may be recoverable"
    WHEN `the right of the buyer or the seller to recover interest in a case where by law interest may be recoverable` THEN JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this Act affects the right of the buyer or the seller to recover interest or special damages in any case where by law interest or special damages may be recoverable"
    WHEN `the right of the buyer or the seller to recover special damages in a case where by law special damages may be recoverable` THEN JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this Act affects ... the right ... to recover money paid where the consideration for the payment of it has failed"
    WHEN `the right of the buyer or the seller to recover money paid where the consideration for the payment of it has failed` THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the section names three rights.
    WHEN `some other matter under section 54` THEN NOTHING
